From 9dbae121603c989b09a5f791e7c22d3f7019db99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Forst <ensonador@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:27:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] braids.h: a model turned mid-note, and the click it makes
 (MODEL_CHANGE_FADE)

Automating the model knob (TP_E1) on a cane or voile track makes the voice click whenever the
value lands on a different model. The model's whole state is the voice's own: a waveguide line
for pluck, bow, reed and flute, the partials or formants for bell, drum, vowel, choir and
whisper. cn_prep and vo_prep compare the model with the one the state is for and reset it when
they differ: cn_clear zeroes the 1536-sample slot and o[1..15], cn_chunk then strikes, vo_init
zeroes the formants. The output therefore steps from the sounding model's sample to silence
(measured at the change: 0.25 where the bell's own largest step is 0.13, and 0.34 against
whisper's 0.11) before the new model starts from rest. A lock per step re-strikes the note; the
LFO on the engine's first knob, or a lock ramp with SHAPE, does it every couple of chunks.

MODEL_CHANGE_FADE selects what the change does (fm1-base's tools/build.py forwards it; unset,
0, is upstream's):

  0  the reset at once, the click above.
  1  the old model fades out over 3 ms, the switch happens at zero, and the new one fades in
     over 3 ms, so automation stays live across the change at the cost of a short dip in that
     voice. The gain is applied per sample in cn_run/vo_run, and only while a fade is in
     flight: a voice's steady-state cost is unchanged (braids_test's cost table and dsp_hash's
     623 cases are identical in every mode). A new note still takes its model at once, a fade
     is dropped when the note or the voice ends (cn_init/vo_init/cn_strike), and a lock that
     returns to the sounding model during the fade cancels the switch instead of re-striking.
  2  the note keeps the model it began on; the lock's value reaches the next note, which is
     what TP_ENGINE already does. The render is bit-for-bit the render with no change at all.

The fade's state lives in ex[20..22], which cane and voile do not use (synth_t has 112 bytes
spare of 12288 and must not grow): 20 the gain, 21 the phase and the model it is heading for,
22 the step a sample.

tests/host/braids_test.c measures the click instead of only bounding it: a droning bell (cane)
and whisper (voile) change model at eight successive blocks, and the largest step across the
change is compared with each model's own largest step, so there is no machine-specific
threshold. braids_test.sh runs the suite once per mode. Flash: 0 526180 B, 1 526776 B (+596),
2 526536 B (+356); RAM and pool unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
